 406:/workspaces/edgetx-sw/radio/src/targets/taranis/lcd_driver_spi.cpp ****     LCD needs longer time to initialize in low temperatures. The data-sheet
 407:/workspaces/edgetx-sw/radio/src/targets/taranis/lcd_driver_spi.cpp ****     mentions a time of at least 150 ms. The delay of 1300 ms was obtained
 408:/workspaces/edgetx-sw/radio/src/targets/taranis/lcd_driver_spi.cpp ****     experimentally. It was tested down to -10 deg Celsius.
 409:/workspaces/edgetx-sw/radio/src/targets/taranis/lcd_driver_spi.cpp **** 
 410:/workspaces/edgetx-sw/radio/src/targets/taranis/lcd_driver_spi.cpp ****     The longer initialization time seems to only be needed for regular Taranis,
 411:/workspaces/edgetx-sw/radio/src/targets/taranis/lcd_driver_spi.cpp ****     the Taranis Plus (9XE) has been tested to work without any problems at -18 deg Celsius.
 412:/workspaces/edgetx-sw/radio/src/targets/taranis/lcd_driver_spi.cpp ****     Therefore the delay for T+ is lower.
 413:/workspaces/edgetx-sw/radio/src/targets/taranis/lcd_driver_spi.cpp **** 
 414:/workspaces/edgetx-sw/radio/src/targets/taranis/lcd_driver_spi.cpp ****     If radio is reset by watchdog or boot-loader the wait is skipped, but the LCD
 415:/workspaces/edgetx-sw/radio/src/targets/taranis/lcd_driver_spi.cpp ****     is initialized in any case.
 416:/workspaces/edgetx-sw/radio/src/targets/taranis/lcd_driver_spi.cpp **** 
 417:/workspaces/edgetx-sw/radio/src/targets/taranis/lcd_driver_spi.cpp ****     This initialization is needed in case the user moved power switch to OFF and
 418:/workspaces/edgetx-sw/radio/src/targets/taranis/lcd_driver_spi.cpp ****     then immediately to ON position, because lcdOff() was called. In any case the LCD
 419:/workspaces/edgetx-sw/radio/src/targets/taranis/lcd_driver_spi.cpp ****     initialization (without reset) is also recommended by the data sheet.
 420:/workspaces/edgetx-sw/radio/src/targets/taranis/lcd_driver_spi.cpp ****   */
