ARM GAS  /tmp/ccLYcsI2.s 			page 1421


 124:/workspaces/edgetx-sw/radio/src/thirdparty/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****        and APB2).
 125:/workspaces/edgetx-sw/radio/src/thirdparty/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c **** 
 126:/workspaces/edgetx-sw/radio/src/thirdparty/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****     [..] Internal/external clock and PLL configuration
 127:/workspaces/edgetx-sw/radio/src/thirdparty/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****          (#) HSI (high-speed internal), 16 MHz factory-trimmed RC used directly or through
 128:/workspaces/edgetx-sw/radio/src/thirdparty/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****              the PLL as System clock source.
 129:/workspaces/edgetx-sw/radio/src/thirdparty/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c **** 
 130:/workspaces/edgetx-sw/radio/src/thirdparty/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****          (#) LSI (low-speed internal), 32 KHz low consumption RC used as IWDG and/or RTC
 131:/workspaces/edgetx-sw/radio/src/thirdparty/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****              clock source.
 132:/workspaces/edgetx-sw/radio/src/thirdparty/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c **** 
 133:/workspaces/edgetx-sw/radio/src/thirdparty/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****          (#) HSE (high-speed external), 4 to 26 MHz crystal oscillator used directly or
 134:/workspaces/edgetx-sw/radio/src/thirdparty/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****              through the PLL as System clock source. Can be used also as RTC clock source.
 135:/workspaces/edgetx-sw/radio/src/thirdparty/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c **** 
 136:/workspaces/edgetx-sw/radio/src/thirdparty/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****          (#) LSE (low-speed external), 32 KHz oscillator used as RTC clock source.
 137:/workspaces/edgetx-sw/radio/src/thirdparty/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c **** 
 138:/workspaces/edgetx-sw/radio/src/thirdparty/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****          (#) PLL (clocked by HSI or HSE), featuring two different output clocks:
 139:/workspaces/edgetx-sw/radio/src/thirdparty/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****            (++) The first output is used to generate the high speed system clock (up to 168 MHz)
 140:/workspaces/edgetx-sw/radio/src/thirdparty/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****            (++) The second output is used to generate the clock for the USB OTG FS (48 MHz),
 141:/workspaces/edgetx-sw/radio/src/thirdparty/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****                 the random analog generator (<=48 MHz) and the SDIO (<= 48 MHz).
 142:/workspaces/edgetx-sw/radio/src/thirdparty/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c **** 
 143:/workspaces/edgetx-sw/radio/src/thirdparty/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****          (#) CSS (Clock security system), once enable using the macro __HAL_RCC_CSS_ENABLE()
 144:/workspaces/edgetx-sw/radio/src/thirdparty/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****              and if a HSE clock failure occurs(HSE used directly or through PLL as System
 145:/workspaces/edgetx-sw/radio/src/thirdparty/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****              clock source), the System clocks automatically switched to HSI and an interrupt
 146:/workspaces/edgetx-sw/radio/src/thirdparty/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****              is generated if enabled. The interrupt is linked to the Cortex-M4 NMI
 147:/workspaces/edgetx-sw/radio/src/thirdparty/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****              (Non-Maskable Interrupt) exception vector.
 148:/workspaces/edgetx-sw/radio/src/thirdparty/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c **** 
 149:/workspaces/edgetx-sw/radio/src/thirdparty/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****          (#) MCO1 (microcontroller clock output), used to output HSI, LSE, HSE or PLL
 150:/workspaces/edgetx-sw/radio/src/thirdparty/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****              clock (through a configurable prescaler) on PA8 pin.
 151:/workspaces/edgetx-sw/radio/src/thirdparty/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c **** 
 152:/workspaces/edgetx-sw/radio/src/thirdparty/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****          (#) MCO2 (microcontroller clock output), used to output HSE, PLL, SYSCLK or PLLI2S
 153:/workspaces/edgetx-sw/radio/src/thirdparty/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****              clock (through a configurable prescaler) on PC9 pin.
 154:/workspaces/edgetx-sw/radio/src/thirdparty/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c **** 
 155:/workspaces/edgetx-sw/radio/src/thirdparty/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****     [..] System, AHB and APB busses clocks configuration
 156:/workspaces/edgetx-sw/radio/src/thirdparty/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****          (#) Several clock sources can be used to drive the System clock (SYSCLK): HSI,
 157:/workspaces/edgetx-sw/radio/src/thirdparty/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****              HSE and PLL.
 158:/workspaces/edgetx-sw/radio/src/thirdparty/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****              The AHB clock (HCLK) is derived from System clock through configurable
 159:/workspaces/edgetx-sw/radio/src/thirdparty/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****              prescaler and used to clock the CPU, memory and peripherals mapped
 160:/workspaces/edgetx-sw/radio/src/thirdparty/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****              on AHB bus (DMA, GPIO...). APB1 (PCLK1) and APB2 (PCLK2) clocks are derived
 161:/workspaces/edgetx-sw/radio/src/thirdparty/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****              from AHB clock through configurable prescalers and used to clock
 162:/workspaces/edgetx-sw/radio/src/thirdparty/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****              the peripherals mapped on these busses. You can use
 163:/workspaces/edgetx-sw/radio/src/thirdparty/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****              "HAL_RCC_GetSysClockFreq()" function to retrieve the frequencies of these clocks.
